text:
maria-platform: Quick thread 1: can we pick a single contract for client-visible failure details? we keep duplicating logic across SDKs and console.

devin-sdk: TL;DR: prefer a small typed payload (enum + retryable + hint) rather than parsing free-text. SDKs can then expose stable fields and helpers.

zoe-ux: UX wants a guaranteed `ui_hint` field we can surface verbatim to apps (max 100 chars). must be non-sensitive.

tomas-sre: Operationally we need a clear distinction between: quota exhausted (hard block), soft degradation (fallback model served), and transient infra (retryable). These map to different alerts.

james-product: Product note: customers sometimes surface messages to end-users. We shouldn't leak internal quota buckets. `reason_code` should be opaque (e.g. Q-17) and resolvable in console.

maria-platform: Proposal A (status-preserve): keep existing HTTP codes (429/503/500), but add header `X-RW-Reason` and JSON fields: `type` (enum), `retryable` (bool), `ui_hint` (string), `reason_code` (opaque).

devin-sdk: Proposal B (status-first): introduce new distinct 4xx subcodes (danger: proxies) OR use `X-RW-Model` header. I prefer header + body because proxies that rewrite codes still usually pass headers.

zoe-ux: If we use headers, console badges must still derive from body when headers are absent (eg mobile clients behind proxies). Keep failover order: header -> body -> http status.

rachel-legal: Legal: do not include anything that identifies other customers or internal SLAs in `ui_hint`. Also, do not include billing numbers. Mapping to console is fine.

tomas-sre: Telemetry: emit tags `rw.err.class`, `rw.err.type`, `rw.err.reason_code`. All enums only. No free-text in metrics.

maria-platform: Sample payload (header-first fallback-safe):

```
HTTP/1.1 503 Service Unavailable
X-RW-Error: soft_degrade
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "soft_degrade",
  "retryable": true,
  "retry_after": 5,
  "ui_hint": "Performance degraded, a faster model served. Try again or pin model.",
  "reason_code": "D-02"
}
```

devin-sdk: SDK behavior: parse header + body. Expose: error.type (enum), error.shouldRetry() (bool), error.uiMessage() (string), error.reasonCode() (string). Default uiMessage should fallback to short canned templates per type.

james-product: For console: show resolved reason (human-readable) but hide opaque reason codes behind a clickable expand so support can see full bucket.

zoe-ux: Badge mapping idea: green=ok, amber=soft_degrade (tooltip: "fallback used"), red=hard_block (tooltip: "quota hit"). Also show a subtle "customer-facing" text line that is the `ui_hint`.

rachel-legal: Also add a short privacy disclosure on console where we map `reason_code` to internal names, because customers may ask how we categorize quotas.

tomas-sre: Rollout plan: implement header+body, SDKs will be backward-compatible (if missing fields treat as unknown). Canary 5% + debug logs for 2 weeks. Add alert when >1% of traffic has `type=hard_block` for a tenant.

maria-platform: Migration note: clients that only check status code today will continue to work, but recommend SDK upgrade. We'll publish a client migration guide with sample catch blocks.

devin-sdk: Example JS snippet to recommend in migration guide:

```js
try {
  await redwood.request(...)
} catch (err) {
  if (err.type === 'hard_block') {
    // surface friendly message, stop retries
  } else if (err.shouldRetry()) {
    // exponential backoff retry
  } else {
    // fallback logic
  }
}
```

